# Date every lecture

Nik writes the note the **same day** as class. **Date added = class date.** Do not treat “date added” as unknown.

## Calendar
- **25 July 2026:** convocation — no class.
- **26 July–23 August:** **one** class a day, except **15 August** (Independence Day).
- **24 August onward:** **two** classes a day.
- One class may sit in **two files** (two parts). Count as **one**. Known: **10 August** = Early Modern L4 + Early Medieval A1; **23 August** = Early Medieval A3 + Medieval A3.

## When you add or edit a lecture
1. Put the date on the heading: `### Lecture 2 — 1 August 2026` (same style as Geography / History).
2. If the file only has `*Date added: YYYY-MM-DD*`, copy that day onto the Lecture heading.
3. Never leave a new lecture undated. Never invent a date to fill a hole if Nik did not add a note that day.
4. Two-part same-day class: label **(Part 1)** and **(Part 2)** on the headings; do not mark that day as two classes.
